{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-05T17:03:56.805Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"41","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"Confirmed and fixed in 35b86ad6. Reproduced first, and the reproduction was worse than the finding states.\n\nREPRODUCTION. A probe capturing the complete snapshot into memory, then running --force, then calling loadOrDeriveSelectiveSearchSnapshot with that in-memory snapshot:\n\n    generation after --force: \"7b3e20f46f8ae89188245df8686302ba\"\n    derive-from-preload:  hit=true  outgoing=true\n    persisted DerivedFrom=\"7b3e20f46f8ae89188245df8686302ba\"  outgoing=true\n    LATER ordinary query: hit=true  outgoing=true\n\nThe last line is the part that makes it durable: a subsequent selective query holding NO preload at all is served the view derived from the retired snapshot, because it was persisted stamped with the CURRENT generation. This is strictly worse than the race 022caa55 closed - there the late write carried the OUTGOING generation and was unservable; here removeDerivedCacheEntries has already run, so nothing later discards it.\n\nCAUSE, exactly as described. search.go:764 loads the complete snapshot via loadCachedCompleteSearchSnapshot, and only later does loadOrBuildSearchSnapshot read the generation (search_cache.go:245). That inverts the ordering the mechanism rests on, stated in the code at search_cache.go:222-226: 'Read the generation BEFORE any complete snapshot is'. The non-preload path is correctly ordered - the generation is read at :245, the complete entry at :307 - so only the preload parameter bypasses it.\n\nFIX (the finding's second suggestion, 'bind the preloaded snapshot to its generation'; the first, 'reload the complete entry', would have thrown away the optimisation the preload exists for). A preloadedCompleteSnapshot now pairs the snapshot with the generation observed BEFORE it was read, read inside loadCachedCompleteSearchSnapshotBinding ahead of readSearchSnapshot. The selective loader derives from the preload only while that generation is still current; otherwise it discards it and falls through to the on-disk complete entry, which IS read after the generation and stamps correctly. Cost when nothing raced: nothing. Cost when a --force raced: one decode.\n\nAn unreadable marker is reported as generationKnown=false rather than as a failed load, so a broken marker does not cost a complete query its preindex hit - a complete entry is derived from nothing and needs no generation. Only the selective derivation refuses it.\n\nREGRESSION TEST. TestPreloadedCompleteSnapshotIsBoundToItsGeneration (internal/sem/cache_generation_marker_test.go). It asserts the served result, and then the durable half: that an ordinary later query holding no preload is not served the retired view, and that the persisted entry carries the current generation. On a compile-clean revert (restoring the predicate to `if preloadedFull != nil {`; `go build ./...` and `go vet ./internal/sem/` both clean) it fails:\n\n    cache_generation_marker_test.go:356: a preloaded snapshot read under a retired generation was derived from anyway\n    --- FAIL: TestPreloadedCompleteSnapshotIsBoundToItsGeneration (0.44s)\n\nWith the predicate restored: `go test ./internal/sem/` =\u003e ok, 120.465s, and `go test ./...` across the repo exits 0.","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1S6FY8X0S3JJVQQXY2EHFQD","targetId":"01M1S6FY9AP1X8TG1J2E0YMHXT","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M1NE8HTT28JGJ7T5MTW7H75J"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
