{"data":{"actorId":"01KSK3QAE64QAADZ4Z86DY4771","createdAt":"2026-09-04T12:24:44.651Z","eventType":"comment.status_changed","id":"26","payload":{"from":"open","reason":"Fixed on the PR branch (33ef72c9). CONFIRMED: a corrupt or unreadable generation marker was read as the empty pre-generation value, which silently reverted to the racy behaviour the marker was added to prevent — an in-flight derivation against a retired snapshot would be revalidated. Now fails closed: readCacheGeneration returns (string, error), only errors.Is(err, fs.ErrNotExist) maps to ('', nil), and the caller gates both the cached hit and both writeSearchSnapshot sites on generationKnown. Fail-without-fix across three distinct corruption modes: 'an unreadable generation marker was read as the legacy empty generation and revalidated a pre-force derivation'. The converse is pinned too — a genuinely ABSENT marker still hits the legacy generation, and that test passed both before and after.","to":"resolved"},"reviewId":"01M1NN1DK3EX5CCKCBXWVWR9SN","targetId":"01M1NN1DK71QWXTDSPRZNXJ9AQ","targetType":"review_comment","trailId":"01M1NE8HTT28JGJ7T5MTW7H75J"},"event":"comment.status_changed"}
